<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zawi ibn Ziri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1019</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zawi ibn Ziri was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanhaja">Sanhaja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> leader of the Zirid family who came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> to serve the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. During the civil war after 1009 he seized the district of Elvira around 1013 and moved its centre to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Granada. He returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> around 1019, leaving the kingdom to his nephew Habbus.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Around 1013 the Sanhaja Berber leader <b>Zawi ibn Ziri</b>, a veteran of the caliphal wars, took over the district of Elvira and moved its centre to the more defensible hill of Granada.</blockquote><a href="/state/taifa-of-granada">Taifa of Granada</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=36.78,3.06&amp;year=1009" aria-label="Algiers on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4627 838 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Zawi ibn Ziri"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5077 1108h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5077 1108h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=36.78,3.06&amp;year=1009">What was here in 1009? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
